{#- The front door (targum-internal#69, 2026-09-16; rebuilt around one promise 2026-10-01).

    The one page a stranger meets. It is not the desk and not a reader: it carries its
    own bar and its own foot. One spine runs down it: the promise, a box that keeps it,
    then what you can bring, the record of the words you know, the word card, targum in
    Claude and ChatGPT, the library, the Tanakh, the list and the questions.

    The box under the headline is real (targum-internal#399): a pasted link is described
    by `/waitlist/look`, which reads metadata and nothing else — no build, no spend, no
    model — and joining from there keeps the link to hand back in the invitation. It is
    the one part that needs JavaScript, so it is drawn hidden and `landing.js` shows it;
    with JavaScript off the page reads in full and the waitlist below still works.

    Everything it draws is baked in. No script, stylesheet, font or image comes off the
    network, which is the reader's rule (§11) and holds here for the same reason: the
    first page anybody sees should not be a page that phones somebody else first. -#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ page_language|default('en') }}">
<head>
{#- The alternates moved into `_public_head.html.j2` on 2026-09-22, when the text pages
    and the weekly began declaring theirs too. That file's own header says a head kept in
    four copies is four copies that drift, and this was the copy. -#}
{% include '_public_head.html.j2' %}
<style>{{ asset('landing.css') }}</style>
{{ hebrew_face() }}
{#- The Torah's own face, beside the modern one: the ta'amim are boxes without it. -#}
{{ scripture_face() }}
{{ chrome_face() }}
</head>
<body class="landing">
{% with bar_class = 'bar', home = '', here = '/' %}{% include '_front_bar.html.j2' %}{% endwith %}

<main id="top">
  <div class="col">
    <div class="hero">
      <h1>{{ t("landing.door.headline", "Learn Hebrew from anything.") }}</h1>
      <p class="lede">{{ t("landing.door.lede", "Paste a link to a video, a post, an article or a podcast. Or drop in a screenshot. We’ll add the vowels and the English, and explain any word you tap.") }}</p>
    </div>

    {#- The box (targum-internal#399). Hidden until the script is there to run it. -#}
    <section class="try" id="try" aria-labelledby="tryH" hidden>
      <div class="try-head">
        <h2 id="tryH">{{ t("landing.door.try.heading", "Try it.") }}</h2>
        <p>{{ t("landing.door.try.lede", "Paste a link and we’ll tell you what we found.") }}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="box">
        <form class="field" id="tryForm" action="/waitlist/look{% if asked|default('') %}?lang={{ asked }}{% endif %}" method="post" novalidate>
          <input id="tryInput" name="url" type="url" inputmode="url" autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="{{ t("landing.door.try.placeholder", "Paste a link") }}" aria-label="{{ t("landing.door.try.label", "A link to something in Hebrew") }}">
          <button class="btn filled small" type="submit">{{ t("landing.door.try.go", "Go") }}</button>
        </form>
        <div id="tryOut" aria-live="polite"></div>
        {#- Joining from the box: the waitlist's own plain post, carrying the link. Shown
            only once a link has been described, so it is never a form about nothing. -#}
        <form class="keep" id="keep" method="post" action="/waitlist{% if asked|default('') %}?lang={{ asked }}{% endif %}" hidden>
          <input type="hidden" name="from" value="/">
          <input type="hidden" name="link" id="keepLink" value="">
          <h3>{{ t("landing.door.keep.heading", "Join to save it") }}</h3>
          <label class="field">
            <input type="email" name="email" required inputmode="email" autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="email" placeholder="{{ t("landing.page.you-example-com", "you@example.com") }}" aria-label="{{ t("landing.page.your-email", "Your email") }}">
            <button class="btn cta small" type="submit">{{ t("landing.door.keep.join", "Join") }}</button>
          </label>
          <p class="note">{{ t("landing.door.keep.note", "We’ll keep the link and send it back with your invitation.") }}</p>
          <p class="unlock">{{ t("landing.door.keep.unlock", "Then we’ll show you how much of it you already know.") }}</p>
        </form>
      </div>
    </section>

    <p class="lede after-try">{{ t("landing.door.after-try", "Don’t have anything yet?") }} <a href="#library">{{ t("landing.door.after-try.link", "Start with our free library.") }}</a> {{ t("landing.door.after-try.tanakh", "It includes the whole Tanakh.") }}</p>
  </div>

  <section class="part" id="bring">
    <div class="col">
      <div class="part-head">
        <p class="label">{{ t("landing.door.bring.label", "What you can bring") }}</p>
        <h2>{{ t("landing.door.bring.heading", "Copy the link, paste it here.") }}</h2>
        <p>{{ t("landing.door.bring.lede", "It works with most places you’ll run into Hebrew. TikToks stay vertical, and articles get their vowels.") }}</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="doors">
        <li class="door"><span class="mini wide" aria-hidden="true"><b class="pic"></b><i class="m"></i><i class="s"></i></span><span class="name">YouTube</span><span class="how">{{ t("landing.door.youtube.how", "Video on top, text underneath") }}</span></li>
        <li class="door"><span class="mini side" aria-hidden="true"><b class="pic"></b><i class="m"></i><i class="s"></i><i class="m"></i><i class="s"></i></span><span class="name">TikTok</span><span class="how">{{ t("landing.door.tiktok.how", "Stays vertical") }}</span></li>
        <li class="door"><span class="mini side" aria-hidden="true"><b class="pic"></b><i class="s"></i><i class="m"></i><i class="s"></i><i class="m"></i></span><span class="name">Instagram</span><span class="how">{{ t("landing.door.instagram.how", "Reels and posts") }}</span></li>
        <li class="door"><span class="mini side" aria-hidden="true"><b class="pic"></b><i class="m"></i><i class="m"></i><i class="s"></i><i class="s"></i></span><span class="name">Facebook</span><span class="how">{{ t("landing.door.facebook.how", "Reels and videos") }}</span></li>
        <li class="door"><span class="mini post" aria-hidden="true"><b class="dot"></b><i class="m"></i><i class="s"></i><i class="m"></i></span><span class="name">X{% if not x_open %}<span class="soon">{{ t("landing.page.soon", "soon") }}</span>{% endif %}</span><span class="how">{{ t("landing.door.x.how", "Posts") }}</span></li>
        <li class="door"><span class="mini shot" aria-hidden="true"><b class="pic"></b><i class="m"></i><i class="s"></i><i class="m"></i></span><span class="name">{{ t("landing.door.screenshots", "Screenshots") }}</span><span class="how">{{ t("landing.door.screenshots.how", "A chat, a sign, a menu") }}</span></li>
        <li class="door"><span class="mini wave" aria-hidden="true"><span class="bars"><b class="h40"></b><b class="h80"></b><b class="h55"></b><b class="h95"></b><b class="h35"></b><b class="h70"></b><b class="h50"></b><b class="h85"></b><b class="h30"></b><b class="h60"></b></span><i class="m"></i><i class="s"></i></span><span class="name">{{ t("landing.door.files", "Files") }}</span><span class="how">{{ t("landing.door.files.how", "Audio, video or a PDF") }}</span></li>
        <li class="door"><span class="mini news" aria-hidden="true"><i class="h"></i><i class="m"></i><i class="m"></i><i class="s"></i></span><span class="name">{{ t("landing.door.news", "News pages") }}</span><span class="how">{{ t("landing.door.news.how", "Any article") }}</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="part" id="record">
    <div class="col">
      <div class="part-head">
        <p class="label">{{ t("landing.door.record.label", "Your words") }}</p>
        <h2>{{ t("landing.door.record.heading", "We keep track of the words you know.") }}</h2>
        <p>{{ t("landing.door.record.lede", "Every word you learn counts, whatever you read it in. So before you start something new, you can see how much of it you’ll understand.") }}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="record">
        <article class="reader" aria-label="{{ t("landing.door.record.example", "Example: a cooking video you brought") }}">
          <div class="reader-head">
            <span class="thumb" aria-hidden="true"><span class="len tnum">9:04</span></span>
            <div>
              <p class="reader-title">{{ t("landing.page.sabich-step-by-step", "Sabich, step by step") }}</p>
              <p class="reader-meta">{{ t("landing.door.record.meta", "YouTube · 9 minutes · you brought this") }}</p>
              <p class="known"><b class="tnum">80%</b><span>{{ t("landing.door.record.known", "You know 80% of this.") }}</span></p>
              <span class="meter"><i class="p80"></i></span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="lines">
            <p class="line-he">קֹדֶם <span class="w new">מְטַגְּנִים</span> אֶת הַחֲצִילִים עַד שֶׁהֵם <span class="w learning">זְהֻבִּים</span>.</p>
            <p class="line-en">{{ t("landing.door.record.line-1", "First, fry the eggplant until it’s golden.") }}</p>
            <p class="line-he">חוֹתְכִים <a class="w learning" href="#word">עַגְבָנִיָּה</a> וּמְלָפְפוֹן לְסָלָט קָטָן.</p>
            <p class="line-en">{{ t("landing.door.record.line-2", "Cut a tomato and a cucumber for a small salad.") }}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="reader-foot">
            <span class="legend"><i class="l-learning"></i>{{ t("landing.page.working-on-it", "working on it") }}</span>
            <span class="legend"><i class="l-new"></i>{{ t("landing.page.new-to-you", "new to you") }}</span>
            <span>{{ t("landing.door.record.tap", "Tap a word to open its card.") }}</span>
          </div>
        </article>
        {#- Words known over twelve weeks, drawn to one scale. A composed example, like the
            reader beside it; the bars are SVG attributes, which the page's policy allows
            where an inline style is refused. -#}
        {%- set weeks = [620, 760, 880, 1010, 1150, 1260, 1390, 1520, 1660, 1790, 1960, 2140] %}
        <figure class="growth" aria-label="{{ t("landing.door.record.growth", "Example: words known over twelve weeks") }}">
          <div class="growth-top"><b class="tnum">2,140</b><span>{{ t("landing.page.words-known-2", "words known") }}</span></div>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 300 120" role="img" aria-label="{{ t("landing.door.record.growth-said", "Words known rose from 620 to 2,140 over twelve weeks") }}">
            <line x1="0" x2="300" y1="104" y2="104" class="axis"></line>
            {%- for v in weeks %}
            {%- set h = (v / 2400 * 88)|round(1) %}
            <rect x="{{ loop.index0 * 25 + 3 }}" y="{{ (104 - h)|round(1) }}" width="19" height="{{ h }}" rx="2" class="{{ 'now' if loop.last else 'then' }}"></rect>
            {%- endfor %}
            <text x="0" y="118">{{ t("landing.door.record.weeks-ago", "12 weeks ago") }}</text>
            <text x="300" y="118" text-anchor="end">{{ t("landing.door.record.this-week", "this week") }}</text>
          </svg>
          <div class="ledger">
            <div><span class="v tnum">61</span><span class="k">{{ t("landing.page.days-reading", "days on targum") }}</span></div>
            <div><span class="v tnum">48</span><span class="k">{{ t("landing.door.record.texts-finished", "texts finished") }}</span></div>
            <div><span class="v tnum">+1,520</span><span class="k">{{ t("landing.door.record.in-twelve-weeks", "words in 12 weeks") }}</span></div>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="part" id="word">
    <div class="col">
      <div class="part-head">
        <p class="label">{{ t("landing.door.word.label", "The word card") }}</p>
        <h2>{{ t("landing.door.word.heading", "Tap any word.") }}</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="wordpart">
        <aside class="wcard" id="wcard" aria-label="{{ t("landing.page.word-card", "Word card") }}">
          <p class="label">{{ t("landing.page.word-card", "Word card") }}</p>
          <div>
            <p class="word he">עַגְבָנִיָּה</p>
            <p class="sense">{{ t("landing.card.tomato", "tomato") }} <span>· {{ t("landing.card.noun-feminine", "noun, feminine") }}</span></p>
          </div>
          <dl class="facts-list">
            <dt>{{ t("landing.card.from", "From") }}</dt><dd><span class="he">עָגַב</span>, {{ t("landing.door.word.from", "to desire. The tomato was once the love apple.") }}</dd>
            <dt>{{ t("landing.card.plural", "Plural") }}</dt><dd><span class="he">עַגְבָנִיּוֹת</span></dd>
          </dl>
          <div class="story-line">
            <p class="he" id="vowelLine">רַק עַגְבָנִיּוֹת טוֹבוֹת, בָּצָל וְשׁוּם.</p>
            <p class="en">{{ t("landing.door.word.example", "Only good tomatoes, onion and garlic.") }}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card-actions">
            <button class="btn tonal small" type="button" aria-pressed="true" data-state>{{ t("landing.door.word.learning", "Learning") }}</button>
            <button class="btn tonal small" type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-state>{{ t("landing.door.word.know-it", "Know it") }}</button>
          </div>
        </aside>
        <ul class="alsos">
          <li><h3>{{ t("landing.door.word.roots", "Roots") }}</h3><p>{{ t("landing.door.word.roots.said", "Each verb shows its root and the verbs built from it.") }} <span class="he">פָּגַשׁ · נִפְגַּשׁ</span></p></li>
          <li><h3>{{ t("landing.door.word.conjugations", "Conjugations") }}</h3><p>{{ t("landing.door.word.conjugations.said", "The full table, with this form highlighted.") }}</p></li>
          <li>
            <h3>{{ t("landing.page.vowels", "Vowels") }}</h3>
            <p>{{ t("landing.door.word.vowels.said", "Turn them off when you’re ready to read without them.") }}</p>
            <button class="switch" id="swVowels" type="button" role="switch" aria-checked="true"><span class="knob" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ t("landing.page.vowels", "Vowels") }}</button>
          </li>
          <li><h3>{{ t("landing.door.word.both", "Biblical and modern") }}</h3><p>{{ t("landing.door.word.both.said", "It’s one word list. Learn a word in Genesis and it counts when you see it in the news.") }}</p></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {#- targum inside the AI a reader already uses: the cerebral learner's use case, "what
      to read next", answered from their own word list (2026-10-01). The assistant is set
      in type beside targum's own screen, never drawn as Claude's or ChatGPT's interface.
      Only where the connector is open, as everywhere else it is mentioned. -#}
  {%- if connector_is_open() %}
  <section class="part" id="claude">
    <div class="col ask">
      <div class="part-head">
        <p class="label">{{ t("landing.door.claude.label", "In Claude and ChatGPT") }}</p>
        <h2>{{ t("landing.door.claude.heading", "Ask Claude or ChatGPT what to read next.") }}</h2>
        <p>{{ t("landing.door.claude.lede", "Connect targum and it knows your word list. Ask for something to read, and it finds a text just past what you know.") }}</p>
        <dl class="exchange">
          <dt>{{ t("landing.page.you", "You") }}</dt>
          <dd class="q">{{ t("landing.door.claude.question", "Something about cooking I can mostly follow?") }}</dd>
          <dt>{{ t("landing.door.claude.answer-by", "The answer") }}</dt>
          <dd class="a">{{ t("landing.door.claude.answer", "Shakshuka in ten minutes. You know 85% of the words in it.") }}</dd>
        </dl>
        <a class="btn tonal" href="/connect{% if asked|default('') %}?lang={{ asked }}{% endif %}">{{ t("landing.door.claude.connect", "Connect targum") }}</a>
      </div>
      <figure class="phone" aria-label="{{ t("landing.door.claude.screen", "Example: the text it found, on targum") }}">
        <div class="screen">
          <p class="label">{{ t("landing.page.video", "Video") }}</p>
          <span class="thumb wide" aria-hidden="true"><span class="len tnum">10:12</span></span>
          <p class="reader-title">{{ t("landing.page.shakshuka-in-ten-minutes", "Shakshuka in ten minutes") }}</p>
          <p class="known"><b class="tnum">85%</b><span>{{ t("landing.door.claude.known", "You know 85% of this.") }}</span></p>
          <span class="meter"><i class="p85"></i></span>
          <p class="line-he">שָׂמִים שֶׁמֶן בַּמַּחֲבַת וּמְחַכִּים שֶׁיִּתְחַמֵּם.</p>
          <p class="line-en">{{ t("landing.page.put-oil-in-the-pan-and-wait-for", "Put oil in the pan and wait for it to heat up.") }}</p>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>
  {%- endif %}

  <section class="part" id="library">
    <div class="col">
      <div class="lib">
        <div class="part-head">
          <p class="label">{{ t("landing.page.the-library", "The library") }}</p>
          <h2>{{ t("landing.door.library.heading", "Nearly 500 texts and videos, all free.") }}</h2>
          <p>{{ t("landing.door.library.lede", "There’s the news every week at three levels, short stories and poetry. A lot of it is biblical: the whole Tanakh, with the weekly portion read aloud and Onkelos next to the Torah.") }}</p>
        </div>
        {%- if library_open %}
        <a class="btn tonal" href="/library{% if asked|default('') %}?lang={{ asked }}{% endif %}">{{ t("landing.door.library.browse", "Browse the library") }}</a>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
      <ul class="shelf">
        <li class="book"><span class="label">{{ t("landing.door.library.news", "News") }}</span><span class="t">{{ t("landing.door.library.news.t", "This week, in easy Hebrew") }}</span><span class="k">{{ t("landing.door.library.news.k", "Three levels, new every week") }}</span></li>
        <li class="book"><span class="label">{{ t("landing.page.video", "Video") }}</span><span class="t">{{ t("landing.page.shakshuka-in-ten-minutes", "Shakshuka in ten minutes") }}</span><span class="k">{{ t("landing.door.library.video.k", "Subtitled") }}</span></li>
        <li class="book"><span class="label">{{ t("landing.door.library.poetry", "Poetry") }}</span><span class="t">{{ t("landing.page.bialik", "Bialik ·") }} <span class="he">הַכְנִיסִינִי</span></span><span class="k">{{ t("landing.door.library.poetry.k", "With a published translation") }}</span></li>
        <li class="book"><span class="label">{{ t("landing.door.tanakh", "Tanakh") }}</span><span class="t">{{ t("landing.door.library.portion", "This week’s portion") }}</span><span class="k">{{ t("landing.door.library.portion.k", "Read aloud, every week") }}</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="part" id="torah">
    <div class="col torah">
      <div class="part-head">
        <p class="label">{{ t("landing.door.torah.label", "In the library") }}</p>
        <h2>{{ t("landing.door.torah.heading", "The Tanakh, with cantillation marks and Onkelos.") }}</h2>
        <p>{{ t("landing.door.torah.lede", "There’s an English translation under every verse, and Onkelos’s Aramaic when you want it. Tap any word for its root and binyan. Daniel and Ezra’s Aramaic chapters are here too.") }}</p>
      </div>
      <article class="sheet" aria-label="{{ t("landing.page.example-genesis-1-1-3", "Example: Genesis 1:1–3") }}">
        <div class="sheet-head">
          <p class="sheet-title">{{ t("landing.page.genesis-1-bereshit", "Genesis 1 · Bereshit") }}</p>
          <button class="switch" id="swChant" type="button" role="switch" aria-checked="true"><span class="knob" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ t("landing.door.torah.cantillation", "Cantillation") }}</button>
          <button class="switch" id="swOnk" type="button" role="switch" aria-checked="false"><span class="knob" aria-hidden="true"></span>Onkelos</button>
        </div>
        <div class="verse"><span class="num tnum">1</span><p class="v-he" data-chant>בְּרֵאשִׁ֖ית בָּרָ֣א אֱלֹהִ֑ים אֵ֥ת הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם וְאֵ֥ת הָאָֽרֶץ׃</p><p class="v-arc" hidden>בְּקַדְמִין בְּרָא יְיָ יָת שְׁמַיָּא וְיָת אַרְעָא</p><p class="v-en">{{ t("landing.demo.in-the-beginning-god-created-the-heaven-and", "In the beginning God created the heaven and the earth.") }}</p></div>
        <div class="verse"><span class="num tnum">2</span><p class="v-he" data-chant>וְהָאָ֗רֶץ הָיְתָ֥ה תֹ֙הוּ֙ וָבֹ֔הוּ וְחֹ֖שֶׁךְ עַל־פְּנֵ֣י תְה֑וֹם וְר֣וּחַ אֱלֹהִ֔ים מְרַחֶ֖פֶת עַל־פְּנֵ֥י הַמָּֽיִם׃</p><p class="v-arc" hidden>וְאַרְעָא הֲוַת צָדְיָא וְרֵיקַנְיָא וַחֲשׁוֹכָא פָּרַשׂ עַל אַפֵּי תְהוֹמָא וְרוּחָא מִן קֳדָם יְיָ מְנַשְּׁבָא עַל אַפֵּי מַיָּא</p><p class="v-en">{{ t("landing.demo.now-the-earth-was-unformed-and-void-and", "Now the earth was unformed and void, and darkness was upon the face of the deep; and the spirit of God hovered over the face of the waters.") }}</p></div>
        <div class="verse"><span class="num tnum">3</span><p class="v-he" data-chant>וַיֹּ֥אמֶר אֱלֹהִ֖ים יְהִ֣י א֑וֹר וַֽיְהִי־אֽוֹר׃</p><p class="v-arc" hidden>וַאֲמַר יְיָ יְהֵי נְהוֹרָא וַהֲוָה נְהוֹרָא</p><p class="v-en">{{ t("landing.demo.and-god-said-let-there-be-light-and", "And God said: ‘Let there be light.’ And there was light.") }}</p></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="part" id="join">
    <div class="col join">
      <div class="part-head">
        <p class="label">{{ t("landing.page.the-waitlist", "The waitlist") }}</p>
        <h2>{{ t("landing.door.join.heading", "Join the waitlist.") }}</h2>
        <p>{{ t("landing.door.join.lede", "We’re letting people in a few at a time. We’ll email you when it’s your turn.") }}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="join-card">
        {% include '_join_form.html.j2' %}
        <p class="join-note">{{ t("landing.door.join.note", "It’s free to start, and the whole library is open. We only need your email.") }}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="part" id="questions">
    <div class="col">
      <div class="part-head">
        <p class="label">{{ t("landing.page.questions", "Questions") }}</p>
        <h2>{{ t("landing.door.faq.heading", "Before you join.") }}</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq">
        <details><summary>{{ t("landing.page.when-does-it-open", "When does it open?") }}</summary><p>{{ t("landing.door.faq.open", "Soon. We’re letting people in a few at a time. Join and we’ll email you when it’s your turn.") }}</p></details>
        <details><summary>{{ t("landing.page.is-targum-for-me", "Is targum for me?") }}</summary><p>{{ t("landing.door.faq.for-me", "If you’re learning Hebrew and can read the alphabet, yes. It doesn’t matter where you live or why you’re learning.") }}</p></details>
        <details><summary>{{ t("landing.page.biblical-or-modern", "Biblical or modern?") }}</summary><p>{{ t("landing.door.faq.both", "Both. They share one word list, so a word you learn in Genesis counts when it shows up in the news.") }}</p></details>
        <details><summary>{{ t("landing.page.what-will-it-cost", "What will it cost?") }}</summary><p>{{ t("landing.door.faq.cost", "The library is free and will stay free. There’ll be a paid plan for reading your own links.") }}</p></details>
        {%- if connector_is_open() %}
        <details><summary>{{ t("landing.page.can-i-use-it-in-claude-or-chatgpt", "Can I use it in Claude or ChatGPT?") }}</summary><p>{{ t("landing.page.yes-connect-targum-and-your-ai-talks", "Yes. Connect targum and your AI talks to you in Hebrew built from the words you know, and shows you how to fix each mistake.") }} <a href="/connect">{{ t("landing.page.see-how-to-connect", "See how to connect") }}</a></p></details>
        {%- endif %}
        <details><summary>{{ t("landing.page.is-what-i-bring-private", "Is what I bring private?") }}</summary><p>{{ t("landing.page.yes-what-you-bring-is-yours-and-we", "Yes. What you bring is yours, and we never train a model on it.") }}</p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

{% with signin = true %}{% include '_public_foot.html.j2' %}{% endwith %}

{% if strings %}<script>window.TARGUM_STRINGS = {{ strings|tojson }};</script>
{% endif %}<script>{{ asset('strings.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('landing.js') }}</script>
</body>
</html>
